Subject: [PATCH] Repair PR#82 merge, re-land missing kernel-boot fixes,
 complete .code16 branch encoding

AUDIT of PR#82 (.code16 encoding, merged as 9944a63e) vs. my parallel
implementation, empirically byte-diffed against GAS:

VERDICT - PR#82's architecture is BETTER on two points, which I keep:
 1. Central prefix inversion (fixup_code16_prefixes + sized_op) instead
    of my per-site opsize_prefix(size) rewrite of 43 emit sites. One
    place owns mode knowledge; single-encoding instructions (ret/nop/
    cli/int) cannot accidentally gain a 66 because only encoders that
    made a real width choice set sized_op.
 2. encode_abs_addr_modrm unifying eleven bare-label absolute-address
    sites (vs. my label_as_abs_mem + encode_modrm_mem detour).

But the MERGED state was broken and incomplete; this commit fixes:

 a) encode_abs_addr_modrm was CALLED 11x but never DEFINED - main did
    not compile (E0599 x11). Implemented in core.rs: 32-bit mode =
    rm=101 + disp32 + R_386_32; .code16 = rm=110 + disp16 + R_386_16.
 b) encode_modrm_mem had NO .code16 path: `testb $0x80, sym` through a
    Memory operand emitted 32-bit ModR/M + disp32 inside real-mode code
    (silent wrong bytes vs GAS `f6 06 <d16>`). Added the 16-bit table
    (bx/bp/si/di combos, %bp disp8 special case), disp16 absolutes with
    R_386_16, pending_addr32 for 32-bit register bases.
 c) mov $imm32/$sym32, %reg never set sized_op: `movl $0x12345678,%eax`
    in .code16 lost its 66 prefix and decoded as mov $imm16 + stray
    bytes (silent wrong code). Both Integer and Symbol arms marked.
 d) Branches: call/jmp/Jcc in .code16 now emit E8/E9/0F8x rel16 with
    R_386_PC16 (addend -2); `calll` keeps the 66-prefixed rel32+PC32
    form (wakeup_asm.S forces 4-byte return addresses with it). New
    writer hook reloc_pc16() folds same-section locals to constants
    (GAS emits no reloc there); reloc_patch_size() gives 16-bit reloc
    types 2-byte patch slots so a 4-byte write cannot clobber the
    following field.
 e) pushfl/popfl/pushal/popal ('l' = genuine 32-bit form) and
    ret/retl/lretw width-by-suffix in .code16; ljmpl = 66 EA imm32
    seg16 vs ljmp/ljmpw = EA imm16 seg16 (la57/wakeup trampolines).

RE-LANDED fixes that PR#82 did not include (all previously proven,
lost in the reset):
 f) Absolute .set constants: `.set section_count, (. - section_table)
    / 40` (header.S PE metadata) evaluates with `.`-position and
    forward label refs; relocs against such names patch constants.
    Bare-symbol targets stay aliases (asm_label_alias guard).
 g) Cross-section `.byte a - b` emits R_*_PC8 with A = addend +
    byte_off - b_off (header.S `.byte start_of_setup-1f` short jump);
    identical reloc to GAS (bd16.s: .other - 1 PC8).
 h) Pure-constant data expressions probe before the " - " diff split
    (.quad ((0x1000000)+(0x200000-1)) & ~(0x200000-1) = pref_address).
 i) pushw $sym = 68 imm16 + R_386_16 in .code16 (header.S pushw $6f).

Documented deviations (size-optimal forms GAS picks that lccc does
not replicate; semantically identical, byte-larger):
 - GAS relaxes same-section short branches to rel8 (74 fe); lccc emits
   fixed rel16 (0f 84 fc ff) - always in range for real-mode blobs.
 - GAS uses the A1/A3 moffs shortform for mov abs,%eax; lccc emits the
   generic 8B/89 ModR/M form (1 byte larger).

PROOF: c16full.s probe (60+ instruction shapes incl. branches, far
jumps, prefixes, 16-bit ModR/M, relocs) - remaining GAS diff is
exactly the two documented deviations. st16.s/bd16.s/qx.s/pw.s
byte- or reloc-identical to GAS.

